  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/rSOjX6NftLop_5iKre_FmfY3JPXaOHon4ppyxv_pBBs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nVertex of triangle is $(1,1)$ and midpoint of sides through this vertex is $(-1,2)$ and $(3,2)$ $\\Rightarrow$ vertex $B$ and $C$ come out to be $(-3,3)$ and $(5,3)$\n$\\therefore$ centroid is $\\frac{1-3+5}{3}, \\frac{1+3+3}{3}$ $\\Rightarrow(1,7 / 3)$",
